{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And He brought me up</b> — by way of parable, for I was in my lowliness among the evils that surrounded me, the enemies." "Some say: <b>שאון</b> — from the root שואה. And the correct view: <b>שאון</b> [roar] of many waters or of mire, and the <i>heh</i> of יון serves secondarily [as a connective], like <b>את יום השביעי</b>; and it has no parallel except in יון מצולה [the roaring of the deep], murky waters and thick mire." "<b>And He mentioned rock</b> — in contrast to <b>pit</b>." "<b>And established my steps</b> — to ascend onto the rock."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {1 "The text of the second half is difficult: the syntax and the comparison to את יום השביעי are opaque; translated hyper-literally as the witnesses stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:22.178585007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}